        "type": "thinking",
        "thinking": "I'm analyzing अररसन्त as a luṅ (aorist) form, ātmanepada, third person plural — tracing it to a root like रासृ (\"to sound/resound\"), which is ṛdit and bhvādi ātmanepada, and checking how the reduplicated aorist formation applies given the special rule for ṛdit roots.\n\nActually I'm reconsidering: this looks more like it belongs to the curādi root रस (\"आस्वादनस्नेहनयोः\" — to taste/relish), since curādi roots take ṇic and form caṅ-aorist. The parasmaipada would be अररसत्, and since curādi roots are ubhayapada (due to the ṇic causing णिचश्च), the ātmanepada अररसन्त fits well — with the अल्लोप preventing sanvadbhāva so the reduplication stays as र rather than रि.\n\nFor āśīrliṅ ātmanepada, following the pattern of चोरयिषीरन्, the third person plural would be रसयिषीरन् — seṭ with iṭ and सीयुट्.\n\n",
